      "math_academy_id": "q-89139",
      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$",
      "worked_solution": "We can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-(1-{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
